+# APEX Connect — Nginx + Next.js double redirect correction and isolated rollback rehearsal
+
+Date: 14 October 2026. Coordinator GitHub issue #4. **No production deployment or production Nginx reload occurred** in this mission.
+
+## A new independently confirmed second source of teacher navigation failure
+
+The **active** Nginx TLS virtual host `/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/apex-api-ssl` contains unconditional `location = /dashboard { return 307 /admin; }` and `location ^~ /dashboard/ { return 307 /admin; }`. These short-circuit the downstream Next.js proxy **before even an authenticated teacher can get the role-aware route**. Production's older Next `next.config.ts` independently has another unconditional dashboard-to-admin redirect. Merely changing the Axios temporary-password bug, or swapping the compiled Next build alone, would not repair Nginx interception. Both layers have to be corrected in one controlled release transaction.
+
+The corrected standalone Connect source at `a67e29ca8c3956e4fbc250f82c7e572294a2a84a` already removes unconditional Next dashboard redirects, preserves teacher password/session fix and result-card privacy. Compiled candidate build `ONDwxEIZlx5onDIKY7wYf` has tested role-aware `/dashboard` fallback; existing live build remains `XI7EvxpUMkKOxK5ByM2BH`. SHA256 live Nginx site at audit: `b425e52917470a1c8355b570097ca6fc22afa1e4d051b6d52d6c7f56bb3b89f9`. SHA256 corrected Connect next.config.ts `f245246c100b35f26646324e35a2f5427b8278636def980530655474684d5d9f`. Active Connect auth proxy stored source SHA `2d4d9be579952c780d09f8ed66f9981a6c6fef40af4042fb842ca9aa38414193` already matches reviewer source.
+
+## Completed isolation: ACTUAL Nginx reloads, not just syntax tests
+
+Built a root-private `/tmp/assps-connect-loopback-nginx-20261014/` with a copied active Nginx TLS virtual host and separately derived root-level Nginx configuration. Only this isolated Nginx instance listened at **127.0.0.1:3017**, and corrected Next.js was served only on **127.0.0.1:3016**. Its database host pointed to an unavailable QA port and its Core upstream to an unavailable QA port, preventing access to real school records. Production PM2, port3000, public port443 and live Nginx configuration were untouched.
+
+1. Nginx private candidate removed both forced dashboard-to-admin blocks and proxied its catch-all upstream to private corrected Next3016. Actual `nginx -t -c <PRIVATE_NGINX_CONF>` PASS. Actual local TLS GET/HEAD route matrix **6/6 PASS**: /login200, /dashboard307 -> /login?next=/admin, /teacher302 login, /api/auth/me401, /auth/change-password200, /teacher/assessments/report-cards302 login. Evidence SHA256 `bda59cec92cde63e9fc6515594332f8a8c0cd2e626e9afa3a3efea95cc2cfe7a`.
+2. Actual isolated TLS traffic rollback rehearsal: replaced ONLY private Nginx site with a loopback copy of original blue production Nginx config, `nginx -t` PASS, `nginx -s reload -c <PRIVATE_CONFIG>` succeeded; private /dashboard immediately returned 307 /admin (baseline behavior reproduced).
+3. Actual isolated forward switch: restored the corrected Green private site, `nginx -t` PASS, `nginx -s reload -c <PRIVATE_CONFIG>` succeeded; private /dashboard again returned **307 /login?next=/admin**. This proves an actual isolated routing transition and its reversal, **NOT** a production rollback or genuine production traffic certification. Full six Green HTTPS route matrix again PASS.
+4. Standard production `nginx -t` remains PASS and production /dashboard still 307 /admin. Production exam9 1,762 real marks and 213 numeric zeros stayed unchanged. Latest independent full-acl private database backup at `/root/assps-release-backups/connect-full-recovery-20261014T164243Z` has a SHA-checked 2,615,368-byte dump and companion no-password role definitions; restored ACL evidence exists from separate Core checkpoint. Backup is private and never uploaded.
+
+## Automated fail-closed route/provenance checks
+
+`scripts/connect/check-nginx-bluegreen-routing-20261014.cjs` checks that original Blue has both dashboard intercepts, that the private Green config removes both, proxies to the isolated Next port, binds only loopback and references Next config free of unconditional dashboard overrides. It never modifies Nginx and does not issue production permission. Independent adversarial cases `scripts/connect/test-nginx-bluegreen-routing-20261014.cjs` **9/9 PASS**. These static checks protect against a future "deploy Next but forget Nginx" regression. They do **not** prove genuine teacher admission/RLS or physical rollback.
+
+## Exact Core-owned live rollout only after authorization
+
+- Re-verify GitHub issue #4 latest Core/Connect source and current binary as of actual cutover. Preserve the original blue Nginx config and active compiled Next release, its PM2 process topology and fresh full ACL/marks backup.
+- Core prepares a clean Green application with Next candidate, real signed Core policy and restricted tenant-specific authenticated session; the 3016 loopback QA service used in this rehearsal is **NOT connected to production data, NOT a deployable authenticated Green**.
+- Have an actually authorized pre-existing school teacher complete password rotation and sign-in through a Core-controlled secure canary. Verify school/subject assignment and inter-school denial with genuine signed actor; do NOT extract a staff password or treat synthetic QA as genuine acceptance.
+- Once all pre-cutover security gates are satisfied and rollback readiness is independently approved, Core selects reviewed exact Next compiled Green and removes both Nginx `/dashboard` forced redirects in the **same atomic public ingress transaction**, updating public `proxy_pass` only to the authenticated, tested Green listener. `nginx -t` before reload; on any failure restore pinned Blue config and rerun route checks. The private loopback Nginx config has deliberately different listener/proxy ports; **never copy it straight into production**.
+- Post-cutover checks use fresh live genuine staff Login → Change → Login → Teacher Dashboard, role/tenant negative checks, signed full Core application traffic, actual public rollback evidence and school mark integrity fingerprint. Record authentic owner-issued proof; only then mark production successful. Full First Term marks publication is **separate HOLD** pending approved exact maxima, official staff grants, independent paper verification and unrecorded-offering review.
+
+No new academic results, approval or credentials were seeded. Source/Green rehearsal success never substitutes for SaaS Core's final authority.
